# RFC #362 desktop.15 · A3 Plan/Build execution modes (server-enforced).
#
# A plan run must never be able to change project state, no matter how the
# model shapes its tool arguments. Enforcement lives at the single choke point
# every built-in runtime passes through (ToolGateway -> AgentTools.execute),
# not in the UI:
#
#  * RunContext gains `mode: 'plan' | 'build'` (default 'build'); the API Turn
#    and Draft payloads accept it, persist it on the user and assistant
#    messages, and thread it into the RunContext.
#  * AgentTools.execute refuses every write for plan runs (execute_command with
#    a canvas/generation/asset command, timeline_package_import, voice_create,
#    voice_delete) with 403 / code 'plan_readonly'; queries and package exports
#    stay allowed so a plan can inspect state. gateway passes run.mode through.
#  * The API localizes the refusal for direct HTTP clients (zh original,
#    ENGLISH_BY_CODE 'Plan mode is read-only. Switch to Build mode, then run
#    this action again.'); the web UI maps the same Chinese detail to a locale
#    string via assistantToolText (assistant.reply.toolPlanReadonly).
#  * Composer toolbar gains a compact Plan/Build radiogroup (aria-checked,
#    disabled while sending); a plan turn's user message carries a 'Plan'
#    badge so the reply's refusal reads as intended.
#  * Browser fixture: an armed write during a plan run is refused through the
#    real ToolGateway (assistantModes / planRefusals in creation-test-health),
#    so the journey proves the server side end-to-end.
#
# Verified: tsc clean, build ok, i18n 3294 keys / 0 problems, work_mode zh+en
# regression PASS, agent_plan_mode zh+en PASS (modes=[build,build,plan,build],
# refusal code=plan_readonly, writes unchanged).
#
